    narrative:
      "Someone covered dinner, so you open your bank app and send your share. Your bank submits a FedNow credit-push instruction. The FedNow Service validates the message and forwards it to your friend's bank, which accepts; FedNow then settles instantly across the two banks' Federal Reserve master accounts. Your friend's bank normally posts the money within seconds, although an accepted-without-posting exception can delay availability. FedNow runs 24/7, so it does not wait for a batch or a business day. The payment is a credit push and is irrevocable once it settles, so the amount and the recipient have to be right before you send.",
    jurisdiction: ["US"],
    primaryRails: ["FedNow"],
    currencies: ["USD"],
    tags: ["fednow", "instant", "p2p", "consumer", "split the bill"],
